    "agent_last_message": "Implemented the tool in [main.cpp](/workspace/output/main.cpp) with the build file in [CMakeLists.txt](/workspace/output/CMakeLists.txt). It streams the input file in one pass, counts lines/words/bytes per the spec, folds words to lowercase for frequency tracking, computes `unique_words`, and writes the JSON report with the top 10 words sorted by count descending then word ascending.\n\nIt builds successfully from `/workspace/output` with `cmake -B build && cmake --build build`. I also checked the main spec edge cases: empty file, no trailing newline, multiple consecutive newlines, case-insensitive counting, alphabetical tie-breaking, and invalid invocation handling. Successful runs return `0`, invalid arguments or unreadable/missing files return `1`, and unexpected internal failures fall through to `2`.",
